  -- The key steps:
  -- 1. G is torsion-free (hypothesis)
  -- 2. Define γ: G → Q, prove γ is injective
  -- 3. Let H = γ(G) ≤ Q. Prove H is square-closed.
  -- 4. If H is cyclic (≅ Z), output (a).
  -- 5. Otherwise, output (b) with H square-closed.
