/-!
## 3. Corollary: classification of Kirchberg algebras (Theorem 1.3)
-/

/--
**Theorem 1.3 (Dadarlat).** A unital Kirchberg algebra D satisfying the UCT
has the automatic triviality property iff D ≅ O2, D ≅ O∞, or D ≅ O∞ ⊗ U
where U is a unital UHF algebra of infinite type.

The proof combines:
  - Theorem 1.1 (fiberwise KK-equivalence criterion)
  - Proposition 4.1 (K0 classification above)
  - Hirshberg-Rørdam-Winter (2007) absorption result
  - [Dadarlat-Winter 2007] trivialization of C(X)-algebras
-/
theorem automatic_triviality_classification
    (D : Type*) [CstarAlgebra D] [NuclearAlgebra D] [UCTSatisfies D]
    (h_aut_triv : AutomaticTriviality Holds D) :
    (D ≅₂ CuntzAlgebra 2) ∨ (D ≅ₒ CuntzAlgebra ∞) ∨
    (∃ (U : Type*) [UHFAlgebra U] [InfiniteType U], D ≅ CuntzAlgebra ∞ ⊗ U) := by
  -- This is the capstone theorem. Its proof depends on:
  -- 1. The K0 classification (classification_of_k0)
  -- 2. The isomorphism theorem for Kirchberg algebras (Kirchberg-Phillips)
  -- 3. The automatic triviality ⇒ [X, Aut(D)₀] = {*} for all path-connected X
  -- 4. [X, Aut(D)₀] ≅ KK(Cν, SC₀(X\x₀) ⊗ D)  (Dadarlat, Thm 5.9)
  --
  -- These results require substantial C*-algebra theory (KK-theory, UCT,
  -- Kirchberg-Phillips classification) not yet formalized in mathlib.
  sorry

